      "protocol_valid": true,
      "answer": "## CURRENT STORAGE\nThe desktop and mobile PWA uses **LocalStore** for client persistence: IndexedDB holds inspection records, while an attachment adapter prefers filesystem storage when available and permitted, with an IndexedDB blob fallback.\n\n## DATA RETENTION\nDrafts and photos stay local until the API confirms an authenticated upload. Cleanup is **per attachment**; a failed, ambiguous, or unrelated successful request cannot remove its local copy.\n\n## SUPERSEDED PROPOSAL\nThe proposal to store drafts in browser `localStorage` is no longer current.\n\n## IMPLEMENTATION STATE\nRecord persistence and metadata sync are integrated. The attachment interface is drafted, but its production backends and shared contract tests are unfinished; photos still use a temporary test path.\n\n## NEXT STEP\nImplement backend selection and the shared attachment read/write/delete contract. Test both backends for fallback, reload persistence, and acknowledgement-gated cleanup, then connect the adapter to SyncEngine.",
