      "protocol_valid": true,
      "answer": "## CURRENT STORAGE\n\nThe desktop and mobile PWA uses **LocalStore** for browser persistence. Inspection records are in IndexedDB. The attachment adapter prefers filesystem storage when available and permitted, with an IndexedDB blob fallback.\n\n## DATA RETENTION\n\nKeep each draft and photo locally until the API confirms that item’s authenticated upload. Timeouts, expired sessions, validation errors, and conflicts do not authorize removal. Cleanup is scoped to the acknowledged attachment.\n\n## SUPERSEDED PROPOSAL\n\nThe earlier **localStorage** proposal is no longer current.\n\n## IMPLEMENTATION STATE\n\nRecord persistence and metadata sync are integrated. The attachment interface is drafted, but neither production backend has passed the shared contract tests; photos still use a temporary test path.\n\n## NEXT STEP\n\nImplement adapter selection and both attachment backends. Test the same read, write, delete, reload, permission fallback, and acknowledgement-gated cleanup cases against them. Then connect the adapter to SyncEngine.",
