      "protocol_valid": true,
      "answer": "## CURRENT STORAGE\n\nAtlas uses a browser PWA. **LocalStore** keeps inspection records in IndexedDB. Its attachment adapter will prefer filesystem storage when available and permitted, with IndexedDB blobs as the fallback.\n\n## DATA RETENTION\n\nDrafts and photos stay local until the API confirms their authenticated upload. Cleanup applies only to the acknowledged attachment; failed, uncertain, or interrupted transfers retain their local copies.\n\n## SUPERSEDED PROPOSAL\n\nThe proposal to store everything in browser `localStorage` is no longer current.\n\n## IMPLEMENTATION STATE\n\nIndexedDB record persistence and metadata sync are integrated. The attachment interface is drafted, but the production backends and shared contract tests are unfinished.\n\n## NEXT STEP\n\nImplement backend selection and the shared attachment read/write/delete contract. Test both backends, permission fallback, reload persistence, and acknowledgement-gated cleanup before connecting attachments to **SyncEngine**.",
